# Slim the P1 Air *upload* recovery kernel (images/kernel-recovery.img).
#
# Two kernels come out of the p1-air-source build. The installed one
# (kernel.img, in fpvos-p1-air.fwu) runs the air unit, so it keeps the camera
# capture, ISP and Wave5 encoder. This fragment is for the other one only: the
# recovery a stock unit boots from RAM through the Artosyn HID loader (the
# one-time stock->fpvOS upload, from the browser or the fpvOS Recovery app).
# That kernel only runs the firmware-update service over USB, then the unit
# reboots into the installed kernel; it never touches the camera, the encoder
# or any input device, so those subsystems are dead weight in it.
#
# The HID loader uploads at a hard ~14.6 KiB/s (full-speed, 15-byte frames), so
# this kernel's size is the wait. The outer image stays LZ4 (the vendor
# bootloader only unpacks gz/lzo/lz4); XZ only changes how the kernel stores its
# own built-in initramfs.
#
# Kept: USB gadget (DWC2/ECM/ACM/configfs), MTD/spi-nand, UBI/UBIFS, crypto,
# squashfs + overlayfs - the firmware-update path - and the P1 boot guard.
# NOT in any defconfig: recovery-kernel.sh applies it to a copy of the source
# build's kernel tree (./build.sh p1-air-source recovery), so the installed
# kernel and the .fwu are never slimmed.
# CONFIG_DRM is not set
# CONFIG_FB is not set
# CONFIG_BACKLIGHT_CLASS_DEVICE is not set
# CONFIG_MEDIA_SUPPORT is not set
# CONFIG_SOUND is not set
# CONFIG_SND is not set
# CONFIG_INPUT is not set
# CONFIG_HID is not set
# CONFIG_USB_HID is not set
# CONFIG_KALLSYMS is not set
# CONFIG_IKCONFIG is not set
# CONFIG_FTRACE is not set
# CONFIG_FUNCTION_TRACER is not set
# (no DEBUG_KERNEL: CONFIG_EXPERT selects it)
# CONFIG_DEBUG_FS is not set
CONFIG_RD_XZ=y
CONFIG_INITRAMFS_COMPRESSION_XZ=y
# CONFIG_INITRAMFS_COMPRESSION_GZIP is not set
